# Accounts

> Status: Ready
> Priority: P0
> Depends On: Household
> Next Feature: Transactions

---

# Overview

Accounts represent financial places where money is held in Kin Finance.

Each Account has a name, type, and balance. Accounts help users track where their money lives — cash on hand, bank accounts, e-wallets, or credit cards.

In MVP, each Household has its own set of Accounts. Accounts are created and managed by the Owner. Members can view and use only accounts that are visible to them.

---

# Goals

- Allow users to track multiple financial accounts.
- Support opening balances with automatic initial transaction recording.
- Give Owner control over which accounts Members can see.

---

# Scope

## In Scope

- Create an Account with optional opening balance.
- Edit an Account (name, type).
- Delete an Account.
- List all Accounts visible to the current user.
- Toggle Account visibility for Members.
- Auto-record opening balance as "initial balance" transaction.

## Out of Scope

- Account icons (future).
- Account colors (future).
- Multi-currency (future).
- Account archiving (future).
- Account merging (future).

