# Error State

Show messages that are easy to understand.

Examples:

- Failed to create account.
- Account name already exists.
- Account name is too short.
- Cannot delete account — existing transactions reference this account. Delete or reassign those transactions first.
- Please try again.

Do not show technical backend errors.

---

# Success Criteria

Feature is considered complete when:

- Owner can create an Account.
- Owner can edit an Account name and type.
- Owner can delete an Account.
- Owner can toggle Account visibility.
- Member can only see visible Accounts.
- Member cannot create, edit, delete, or toggle visibility.
- Opening balance is recorded as "initial balance" transaction.
- Account balance auto-updates on transaction changes.
- Member can create transactions on visible Accounts even if balance is hidden.
- Validation works correctly.
- Empty State is available.
- Error State is available.

